WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
 
well well  welcome back maleficent fans disney's  live actions have been taking over the  film industry in full force  including one of their biggest hits  maleficent but if you've ever watched  angelina jolie's maleficent  you know that disney strayed far away  from the plot of the original sleeping  beauty  in this video we'll be taking a look at  just how different the two movies are by  delving behind the scenes of both  which movie really is the better story  and did disney make a mistake with their  live action or was it the change  sleeping beauty needed all along  did you hear that my pen  let's start off with the most basic  difference in the making of the two  films  they're actors of course disney's remake  had hollywood sweetheart angelina jolie  take on the role of maleficent  in the films in sleeping beauty actress  eleanor oddly was cast for the role but  she was no stranger to the disney world  she also voiced lady tremaine in  cinderella making the movie a live  action  of course saved the work of having to  animate angelina jolie but the  production put in the time making her  perfect in another way  she didn't just grow out those sharp  cheekbones overnight angelina spent  hours in hair and makeup while the  artist perfected her look for the film  oddly also spent some time physically  transforming for the role  she had to act out the scenes in costume  in order to help animators portray her  real-life movements  overall their costumes horns and  intimidating looks are pretty similar  next up the one and only princess aurora  of course  the elegant l fanning took on the role  of the cursed princess in the live  action and brought to life a modern  version of let's face it the pretty  bland original version  but there was nothing bland about the  voice behind the animated sleeping  beauty  mary costa took on that role back in the  1950s but another actress  helene stanley was actually the face  behind sleeping beauty  she was the live-action model for the  animation of aurora while helane was  dressed in a real-life costume of what  came across in the animation  elle fanning's version of aurora  included much more variety in her  wardrobe  the similarities between their  appearances stop at their blonde hair  and kind face  now here's what the real big differences  start in the production of the two films  did you ever watch sleeping beauty and  wonder why  exactly maleficent was so mad at the  royals that she would put an evil curse  on their innocent daughter  besides not being invited to the  ceremony there was never really any  reason behind it  i really felt quite distressed and not  receiving an  invitation but in maleficent that all  gets answered  maleficent wasn't exactly evil in the  live action she is only seeking revenge  on aurora's father king stefan  after saving his life he betrays her by  seducing her drugging her and then  cutting off her wings  that is why she became the evil queen of  the moors with a thirst for revenge  the maleficent script definitely gave  the character a more in-depth  personality  and weirdly had a sympathizing with her  despite her evil ways  another fun fact angelina's daughter  actually crashed a brainstorming session  where she helped the screenwriters come  up with an important storyline in a  sequel involving the dark fae  one of the most iconic scenes of the  original movie has to be when maleficent  transforms into a literal fire-breathing  dragon in the final battle against  prince philip  however in the film maleficent that  never happens instead in the live action  maleficent turns her familiar divole  into a dragon instead  another plot twist at the end of those  battles is that in sleeping beauty  maleficent meets her demise  but in maleficent it's king stefan they  take down the closest maleficent ever  comes to transforming into a dragon is  in maleficent mistress of evil when  aurora's tears resurrect her from the  ashes as a phoenix  speaking of maleficent's familiar there  are huge differences between him and the  two worlds  in sleeping beauty he's the classic evil  sidekick sitting on her shoulder and  doing her dirty work he's also strictly  a crow  while in maleficent he's all those  things we mentioned above let's just say  he's more of a character  not only does he get a name dival but  maleficent has the power to transform  him into a human when needed  his human version is played by sam riley  and while he might have human features  the filmmaker still made sure he kept  his dark crow vibes  we can't forget his rendezvous as a  dragon as well  while the actors and storyline are  definitely very important when making  sure you produce an amazing movie  there's something else that needs to be  perfect to bring  everything to life the set and scene  production considering one movie was  animated and the other a live action  their approach to get that perfection  was of course very different  in the case of sleeping beauty disney  and walt himself hired an artist that  would illustrate the scenes before any  animating happened in fact walt was very  adamant that sleeping beauty's  illustrations had to translate perfectly  after he believed some of his past  movies illustrations never got  translated on screen properly  if you take a look at behind the scenes  filming of maleficent most of the time  the actors are working on a set that  consists of multiple green screens  vfx and cgi were the true winners of the  film if it wasn't for them  the film would not have been able to be  brought to life the way it was  like any good fairy tale movie the day  is saved by true love's kiss in both  films  but even that part of the story is  altered when it comes to maleficent  in sleeping beauty it's prince philip  who swoops in kisses her and breaks the  dreadful sleeping curse  however in maleficent it's maleficent  herself that breaks the curse because of  her love for aurora  instead of waiting for the day where she  would finally get her revenge like in  sleeping beauty  in the live action maleficent grew fond  of aurora referring to herself as her  godmother and even trying to secretly  find a way to stop aurora's impending  doom  overall though both true love's kiss  scenes were filmed and set pretty  similarly  like we mentioned before king stefan is  the reason why maleficent is seeking  revenge in the first place  however not only did he drug and rip off  her wings but he also ended up lying his  way into royalty and stealing the throne  that's right unlike king stefan's  nobility in sleeping beauty he started  off as an evil peasant and orphan who  betrayed many  the differences in their physical  appearances are definitely worth noting  as well  while maleficent's love is what breaks  the curse in the live action it doesn't  mean prince philip wasn't important in  the maleficent films  in sleeping beauty prince philip is your  classic disney prince he's betrothed to  aurora the moment she is born and  happens to spontaneously fall in love  with her at first sight  he's even got the traditional prince  look royal steed and all  while in maleficent he still has royalty  vibes with his sandy hair and horse  their love story is completely different  they are taken with each other during  their first meeting but they go through  more of a courting process and don't  even get engaged until the sequel  what would the story of princess aurora  be without her fairy godmothers  probably not as entertaining let's be  real while in both sleeping beauty and  maleficent their purpose is the same  raise and protect aurora their names and  appearances are slightly different  to start in sleeping beauty the  protectors go by the names flora fauna  and meriwether  in maleficent they're called thistle wit  flittle and not grass  the original film also made sure that  the fairies were presented as super  fantastical with glitter big dresses and  magic wands  but in maleficent they were more one  with nature they all still had their own  color but were more understated fairies  they were also part of maleficent's very  very complicated history  shout out to actresses juno temple  imelda staunton and leslie manville for  bringing the live-action versions to  life  let's be real angelina definitely  brought a whole new level of awesome to  maleficent with her impeccable acting  skills and piercing eyes  there's no comparing but she didn't  bring the awesomeness to maleficent  alone the filmmakers took an old disney  character and made her into an icon  one way they did this was through her  powers in sleeping beauty in addition to  her evil powers  she can transport using a type of spin  magic we gotta admit  it looked pretty cool for a 1950s film  but in maleficent she had wings which  meant she could fly  and oh can she fly in fact her getting  her wings cut off is what gets the  entire plot of the franchise going  it's also pretty interesting to get a  look behind the scenes of how they made  these powers come to life in each film  there's no doubt that tons of hours and  hard work went into the making of these  films despite their differences  it's also changed the way we watch these  films now knowing just what went into  them behind the scenes  were any of these behind the scenes  changes shocking to you let us know if  you prefer maleficent or sleeping beauty  in the comments section below  don't forget to give this a thumbs up  and hit that subscribe button for more  of these fairy tale videos  catch you in another kingdom  you

